---
import ActivityGuideLayout from '../layouts/ActivityGuideLayout.astro';
import ActivityOperators from '../components/ActivityOperators.astro';
const sections = [{ id: 'nearby', label: 'Ahnd & Pakin' }, { id: 'farther', label: 'Farther islands' }, { id: 'arrangements', label: 'Arrange a visit' }];
---
<ActivityGuideLayout page="outer-atolls" title="Pohnpei’s Outer Islands | Ahnd, Pakin & Planning Farther Journeys" description="Distinguish Ahnd and Pakin from Pohnpei’s farther outer islands. Read sourced context and plan permissions, transport, hosting and return arrangements." sections={sections}>
  <section slot="hero" class="tg-section bg-sand"><div class="tg-wrap grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-10 md:gap-16 items-center"><div><p class="tg-eyebrow">Pohnpei State / Beyond the main island</p><h1 class="font-headline text-5xl md:text-7xl lg:text-8xl leading-[1.02] tracking-tight mb-7">Outer<br /><em class="text-ochre-deep">islands.</em></h1><p class="tg-copy">Each journey begins with the people who live there and the people who can take you. Start by distinguishing nearby atolls from farther communities, then plan the visit together.</p><a href="#nearby" class="tg-button bg-basalt text-sand hover:bg-lagoon mt-7">Get your bearings ↓</a></div><div class="aspect-[16/9] overflow-hidden bg-sand-deep"><img
              class="w-full h-full object-cover"
              src="https://res.cloudinary.com/doruy2kdr/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto,c_fill,g_auto,w_1200,h_675/chapter-03-outer-atolls.jpg"
              alt="Aerial view of Pohnpei's outer atolls"
              loading="lazy"
            /></div></div></section>
  <section id="nearby" class="tg-section bg-sand-bright"><div class="tg-wrap"><div class="tg-split mb-10"><div><p class="tg-eyebrow">01 / The nearer atolls</p><h2 class="tg-title">Ahnd &amp; Pakin.<br /><em>Different journeys.</em></h2></div><p class="tg-copy">These atolls lie beyond Pohnpei’s lagoon. An outing involves an ocean crossing and arrangements at the destination. Proximity alone does not establish whether a day trip will work.</p></div><div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12"><article><h3 class="font-headline text-3xl mb-4">Ahnd <span class="text-xl text-basalt/65">/ also written Ant or And</span></h3><div class="tg-copy"><p>Ahnd lies southwest of Pohnpei. Its islands and lagoon are privately owned; discuss permission before travelling. Avoid assuming an empty beach is open to visitors.</p><p>Ask where a boat can take you, who has agreed to receive you and whether the weather allows the planned return.</p></div><p class="tg-source"><a class="tg-link" href="https://www.pohnpei-adventure.com/atolls/">Eco-Adventure: Ahnd &amp; Pakin ↗</a></p><div class="tg-note mt-6"><p class="tg-copy">The Eco-Adventure Guide names Pohnpei Surf Club for Ahnd trips. This is a published connection; confirm current service and permission arrangements directly.</p><ActivityOperators place="ahnd" /></div></article><article><h3 class="font-headline text-3xl mb-4">Pakin</h3><div class="tg-copy"><p>Pakin lies northwest of the main island and has a resident community. Its reef lacks a conventional navigable passage into the lagoon, making arrival more complicated than a routine boat transfer.</p><p>Ask for a boat operator with specific Pakin experience and establish a host contact. Discuss landing conditions, permissions and the return before committing.</p></div><p class="tg-source"><a class="tg-link" href="https://www.pohnpei-adventure.com/atolls/">Eco-Adventure atoll guide</a> · <a class="tg-link" href="https://visitpohnpei.travel/pohnpei-outer-atolls/">Tourism office overview</a></p><p class="tg-note tg-copy mt-6">For help finding an appropriate contact, <a class="tg-link" href="https://visitpohnpei.travel/contact-us/">ask the Pohnpei Tourism Office</a> about your intended destination.</p></article></div><p class="tg-source mt-10">Looking for an island within the lagoon instead? The <a class="tg-link" href="https://www.pohnpei-adventure.com/islands/">Eco-Adventure islands overview</a> distinguishes lagoon islands from the atolls beyond.</p></div></section>
  <section id="farther" class="tg-section bg-sand"><div class="tg-wrap tg-split"><div><p class="tg-eyebrow">02 / Farther across the state</p><h2 class="tg-title">Give the journey<br /><em>its own plan.</em></h2><p class="tg-copy">The tourism office advises planning months ahead. Transport may involve a ship, charter boat or small aircraft, depending on the island. A listed transport option is not a current schedule.</p><p class="tg-source">Source for these island and transport summaries: <a class="tg-link" href="https://visitpohnpei.travel/pohnpei-outer-atolls/">Official outer-island guide ↗</a></p></div><dl class="tg-rows tg-copy"><div><dt>Mwoakilloa (Mokil) &amp; Pingelap</dt><dd>Inhabited atolls east of Pohnpei. The tourism office describes small-aircraft and ship options; ask what is operating for your dates and who can arrange your stay.</dd></div><div><dt>Sapwuahfik (Ngatik)</dt><dd>An atoll southwest of Pohnpei. Ask about both the journey to the atoll and onward boat transfers when discussing air or ship arrangements.</dd></div><div><dt>Nukuoro &amp; Kapingamarangi</dt><dd>Farther south, these communities have distinct Polynesian languages and cultural traditions. The tourism office describes ship-based access; Nukuoro has no airstrip.</dd></div><div><dt>Oroluk &amp; Minto Reef</dt><dd>Remote destinations requiring specialized arrangements. Treat these as separate inquiries, not routine additions to a holiday itinerary.</dd></div></dl></div></section>
  <section id="arrangements" class="tg-section bg-sand-bright"><div class="tg-wrap tg-split"><div><p class="tg-eyebrow">03 / Arrange a visit</p><h2 class="tg-title">Confirm the welcome.<br /><em>Plan the return.</em></h2><p class="tg-copy">Ask the tourism office for an introduction appropriate to the island. Caroline Islands Air is listed for outer-atoll flights; confirm your specific destination, capacity, date and return directly.</p><ActivityOperators service="flights" /><p class="tg-source">Service listing: <a class="tg-link" href="https://visitpohnpei.travel/tour-operators/">Pohnpei Tourism Office ↗</a>. No specific island route is implied by this contact.</p></div><div><h3 class="font-headline text-3xl mb-5">Before you commit</h3><ul class="tg-list tg-copy"><li>Agree on a local host, visitor permission and expectations for dress, photography and activities.</li><li>Confirm transport both ways, including transfers, luggage and what happens if a departure changes.</li><li>Arrange somewhere to stay and establish what food, drinking water and other supplies to bring.</li><li>Ask about communications and assistance at your destination. Share your itinerary and the local contact with someone on the main island.</li><li>Agree the complete price and payment terms before paying. Keep time between your return and onward travel.</li></ul><a href="https://visitpohnpei.travel/contact-us/" class="tg-button bg-basalt text-sand hover:bg-lagoon mt-7">Ask official tourism for help ↗</a></div></div></section>
</ActivityGuideLayout>
